umbs/elmshorn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Elmshorn</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Elmshorn is a town in the Pinneberg district of Schleswig-Holstein, on the Krückau about 30 km north-west of Hamburg.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/eloy-alfaro"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eloy-alfaro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Eloy Alfaro</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Eloy Alfaro was the leader of Ecuador's Liberal Revolution of 1895 and president from 1895 to 1901 and from 1906 to 1911.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/eluru"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eluru.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Eluru</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Eluru is a city in Andhra Pradesh, India, in the delta region between the Godavari and Krishna rivers.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/elusa"><span class="enc-name">Elusa</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Elusa, modern Eauze in the Gers department of south-western France, was the chief town of the Elusates, an Aquitanian people.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/elwell-otis"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elwell-otis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Elwell Otis</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Elwell Otis was a United States Army general who served as military governor of the Philippines from 1898 to 1900.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ely-ocarroll"><span class="enc-name">Ely O'Carroll</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ely O'Carroll was a Gaelic lordship in the Irish